        "eyebrow": "The technology",
        "heading": "The mechanism, not the claim.",
        "body": "<p>\u201cWaterproof\u201d is a word anybody can print on a label. This is what is underneath ours, so you can judge it rather than take our word.</p>"
      }
    },
    "membrane": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "paper",
        "layout": "prose",
        "eyebrow": "The membrane",
        "heading": "Porelle\u00ae is not a name we invented.",
        "prose": "<p>The waterproof layer is Porelle\u00ae, a licensed third-party waterproof-breathable membrane. That distinction matters more than it sounds: a membrane you can look up is a membrane someone else has to stand behind. Water cannot get through it; vapour from the foot can. It is PFOA free.</p><p>Brands that do not name their membrane are asking you to trust an unnamed laminate. We would rather you checked ours.</p>"
      }
    },
    "layers": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "wash",
        "layout": "list",
        "numbered": true,
        "heading": "Three layers, and what each one is for"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Inner layer",
            "body": "<p>Next to the skin.</p><p>A soft knitted lining that moves sweat off the foot and stops the membrane sitting against the skin.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Porelle\u00ae membrane",
            "body": "<p>The waterproof barrier.</p><p>A licensed third-party waterproof-breathable membrane \u2014 not a name we invented. Water cannot get in; vapour from the foot can get out. PFOA free.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Outer layer",
            "body": "<p>Wear surface.</p><p>The knitted face that takes the abrasion inside a boot or shoe, and holds the sock's shape when it is not being worn.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2",
        "i3"
      ]
    },
    "testing": {
      "type": "centre-note",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "paper",
        "heading_size": "h3",
        "eyebrow": "How this is tested",
        "heading": "We publish no test figures yet.",
        "body": "<p>Independent test data is the only kind worth printing, and we do not have it yet. Rather than quote a hydrostatic head or a breathability rating we cannot evidence, we name the membrane and let you look it up.</p>",
        "footnote": "When independent figures exist they will be published here with the name of whoever produced them."
      }
    },
    "wont": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "blue",
        "layout": "list",
        "numbered": false,
        "heading": "What it will not do",
        "head_note": "<p>Every brand tells you what their socks do. This is the other half.</p>"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "They are not a boot replacement.",
            "body": "<p>One component of a system. If your footwear is wrong for the ground, this will not fix it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Water over the cuff gets in.",
            "body": "<p>A sock is open at the top. Go deeper than the cuff and you are wet, and no waterproof sock behaves otherwise.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "They are not indestructible.",
            "body": "<p>A membrane is a membrane. Abrasion, toenails and the wrong wash cycle will eventually end one.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i4": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Breathable does not mean dry inside.",
            "body": "<p>Work hard enough and you will sweat faster than any membrane can move vapour. Breathability slows that. It does not repeal it.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
